<title>GERMANY: Waigel stands by forecast of 2.5 pct 1997 growth.</title>
<headline>Waigel stands by forecast of 2.5 pct 1997 growth.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance Minister Theo Waigel stands by the government's official forecast of 2.5 percent economic growth this year, despite an unclear earlier statement, a Finance Ministry spokeswoman said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Waigel misspoke in a television interview taped for later broadcast when he said growth would be &quot;two-point-two-and-a-half-percent&quot;, the spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>&quot;He meant two-and-a-half percent,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn Newsroom, 4922826097150</p>
